{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '115,145p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/artifact_ref.go; rg -n '\"'^##|D1[45]|operations|producer|resolver'\"' .pose/adr/2026-11-03-governance-reads-use-bounded-operation-scoped-views.md | tail -n 16; sed -n '360,380p' .pose/adr/2026-11-03-governance-reads-use-bounded-operation-scoped-views.md\"","aggregated_output":"// WithSpecSnapshots returns a resolver whose stores read each project's specs\n// once for the rest of the operation.\nfunc (r ArtifactResolver) WithSpecSnapshots() ArtifactResolver {\n\tr.snapshots = &sync.Map{}\n\treturn r\n}\n\n// withSpecSnapshot gives a store the operation's one spec listing of its project, when the\n// resolver carries snapshots; without them the store is returned as it is.\nfunc (r ArtifactResolver) withSpecSnapshot(project string, s Store) Store {\n\tif r.snapshots != nil {\n\t\tsnapshot, _ := r.snapshots.LoadOrStore(project, &specSnapshot{})\n\t\ts.specs = snapshot.(*specSnapshot)\n\t}\n\treturn s\n}\n\nfunc (r ArtifactResolver) Resolve(localProject, raw string) ArtifactResolution {\n\treturn r.resolve(localProject, raw, map[string]bool{}, 0)\n}\n\nfunc (r ArtifactResolver) resolve(localProject, raw string, redirectPath map[string]bool, redirectDepth int) ArtifactResolution {\n\tout := ArtifactResolution{SchemaVersion: 1}\n\tref, err := ParseArtifactRef(raw)\n\tif err != nil || !filepath.IsLocal(ref.Slug) {\n\t\tout.State = \"invalid-artifact-reference\"\n\t\treturn out\n\t}\n\tif ref.Project == \"\" {\n\t\tref.Project = localProject\n\t}\n250:reads of immutable Git objects whose bytes a producer only hashes, is a\n254:## Streamed object reads restore the captured-input budget (D11) — 2026-11-14\n257:read whose bytes a producer only hashes (the `git show --binary` of each\n258:commit that feeds a change set's diff digest) is streamed into the producer:\n268:512 MiB. Measured on the pose-dist corpus, `pose index` runs two operations:\n275:## A coordinator checks the consumed index's inputs for its scopes (D12) — 2026-11-15\n288:computed once per (root, generation, producer), through the coordinator's\n302:## The index's federated material is kept with its read closure (D13) — 2026-11-16\n305:operations. Every review operation checks that the index it reads is\n317:requested store's root, the same base binding and roots, with the resolver\n327:the engine, the project, the store root and the resolver's registry (its\n337:## The review ledger is read once per operation (D14) — 2026-11-16\n356:operations.\n364:## A federated dependency is proved once per operation (D15) — 2026-11-17\n366:Spec `pose-federated-source-proof-is-computed-once-per-operation`. After D14\n372:for each producer, by the same per-operation memo as the review ledger, and\n`git log -1 -- <path>` commands, 81 s. A commit-graph with changed-path Bloom\nfilters takes each from 47 ms to 2 ms and the first call to 59 s; it is\nrepository maintenance, not part of this decision.\n\n## A federated dependency is proved once per operation (D15) — 2026-11-17\n\nSpec `pose-federated-source-proof-is-computed-once-per-operation`. After D14\nthe first closeout call on harne8 still spent about 37 s of CPU in\n`federatedSourceProof`: 64 proofs in one call, 39 of them distinct, because\nseveral roadmaps consume the same pose-dist dependency. The proof reads\nthrough the operation's view, so within the operation it is a function of\nthose reads; it is now kept per source root, identity and pinned revision,\nfor each producer, by the same per-operation memo as the review ledger, and\ncallers receive deep copies. The first call fell from about 80 s to 60 s.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
